H63 — the admission gate: does anything fail when it is removed?

SUITE ARMS
  control                 66 pass /  0 fail   roster-related red: NONE
  roster gate DELETED     66 pass /  0 fail   roster-related red: NONE
  exact match -> substr   66 pass /  0 fail   roster-related red: NONE

LAUNCHER ARMS (the gate itself, driven)
  unrostered + roster    rc=1  reached_claude=False  said_roster=True
  rostered (control)     rc=0  reached_claude=True  said_roster=False
  roster ABSENT          rc=0  reached_claude=True  said_roster=True
  substring of rostered  rc=1  reached_claude=False  said_roster=True
  substring, grep -q     rc=0  reached_claude=True  said_roster=False

FA  suite reds with the roster gate DELETED:      NONE — the gate is unfalsified by the suite
FA' suite reds with exact match loosened:         NONE — the exactness is unprotected
FB  unrostered, roster present: rc=1, reached_claude=False, names the roster=True
FC  roster ABSENT:              rc=0, reached_claude=True, warned=True
FD  `ok` against roster `ok-1`: rc=1, reached_claude=False   (with grep -q: rc=0, reached=True)

  FA FIRED: the whole admission gate can be deleted and the suite stays green.
  FB did not fire: the gate refuses an unrostered callsign and names the roster.
  FC MEASURED: with roster.txt absent the launcher launches ANY callsign — the admission gate fails OPEN on a missing input, and the only signal is a warning line.
  FD did not fire, and `grep -qx` is what stops it: with `grep -q` the same callsign is admitted, so the exactness is load-bearing and needs a check that fails when it goes.
